# Codex permission rules. Tracked deliberately: an untracked allow-list is per-machine, so
# two operators get different agent behaviour from the same task.
# Mirrors TIER 1 of the STANDING AUTHORIZATION block on every chart-backlog bead. Tiers 2 and 3
# are per-bead grants and human gates, deliberately NOT here; baking them into a machine-wide
# prefix rule erases the distinction.
#
# THE BAR IS "BOUNDED AND RECOVERABLE", NOT "READ-ONLY AND HERMETIC". Every header here asserted
# the latter until 2026-08-31 and it was false of nearly every file: most of these rules reach
# the network, and several WRITE. Each file states its own writes below. Nothing here pushes a
# git ref, mutates a cloud provider or a cluster, or merges a PR -- but bd DOES write shared
# state, so read bd.rules before assuming a grant is local.
#
# A rule constrains a command's PREFIX and nothing else -- never a flag, path or refspec that
# appears later in argv. If you cannot express the safe subset as a prefix, do not write the
# allow. Every defect found in review was a comment asserting an invariant prefix matching
# cannot enforce.
# Added 2026-08-31.
# Network, read-only against GitHub.
# PR and run reads. gh pr merge, release and secret writes are deliberately absent.
#
# REMOVED 2026-09-01: gh api -X GET. MEASURED, not theorised -- `-X` and `--method` are the same
# pflag, so the LAST value wins: `gh api -X GET --method DELETE <endpoint>` sends DELETE. Proven
# with GH_DEBUG=api pointed at 127.0.0.1, whose request line read `DELETE /api/v3/...` while a
# plain `-X GET` control read `GET`. A prefix cannot forbid a later --method, so the allow is
# gone. An implicit-GET `gh api <endpoint>` already prompted and still does.
#
# REMOVED 2026-09-01: "create" from the gh pr union. Creating a pull request is a remote write,
# and the tier model this file mirrors names gh pr create as explicitly NOT tier 1.
prefix_rule(pattern=["gh", "pr", ["view", "list", "diff", "checks", "status"]], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["gh", "run", ["view", "list"]], decision="allow")
